Chapter: DiskInspectTest
  cites Dev chapter DiskInspector
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter FactLog
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256

 The disk inspector against the partitioned fixture, which is the disk the
 inspector exists for: an ESP at LBA 34..127 and a fact-store partition at
 128..222 on a 256 sector medium.

 THE FIXTURE IS WHY base 128 MEANS ANYTHING. A store that still addressed
 absolutely would answer 0, and 0 is also what a raw unpartitioned disk
 legitimately answers, so a fixture with the store at the bottom could not
 tell the two apart. That is the same reason facts-partition uses this
 disk, and it is why the inspector is tested here rather than against a
 blank image.

 `cmp-differ` IS A STATEMENT ABOUT THE ALLOCATOR, not about the disk.
 `block-read-sector` takes the current heap pointer as its destination and
 bumps it, so two reads land on two distinct buffers and a comparison
 needs no snapshot between them. If it reused one buffer instead, the
 second read would overwrite the first and sectors 0 and 1 -- a protective
 MBR and a GPT header, which cannot be equal -- would compare identical.
 So this line fails loudly if that property ever changes.

 `cmp-same` reads the same sector twice and must be identical. Without it
 a comparison hardwired to "differ" would pass on the line above, and it
 is also what proves the loop traverses the whole sector: reporting
 "identical over 512 bytes" requires reaching index 512, so the counter
 the offset is read from is exercised end to end.

 We say:

Section: Joining

  joined : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  joined (xs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else if text-length acc == 0 then joined xs (i + 1) (list-at xs i)
    else joined xs (i + 1) (acc & " | " & list-at xs i)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    let r = fact-store-region
    in let before = di-superblock-lines r
    in let store = disk-load
    in let written = disk-write-fact store DefinitionFact "inspect-me" 7
    in let flushed = disk-checkpoint written
    in let after = di-superblock-lines r
    in let facts = di-facts-report 64
    in act
      sc <- di-sector-count-line
      print-line-uni ("sectors: " & sc)
      print-line-uni ("direct: " & di-region-line r)
      print-line-uni ("sb-before: " & joined before 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("count: " & show (disk-fact-count flushed))
      print-line-uni ("sb-after: " & joined after 0 "")
      print-line-uni ("facts: " & joined facts 0 "")

      d <- di-compare-line 0 1
      print-line-uni ("cmp-differ: " & d)

      s <- di-compare-line 1 1
      print-line-uni ("cmp-same: " & s)

      dump <- di-sector-lines 1
      print-line-uni ("dump-head: " & list-at dump 0)
      print-line-uni ("dump-row0: " & list-at dump 1)
    end
  end
